  "body": "Closes #980\nClaim: cloud/fb-quickwins-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/fb-quickwins-sonnet)\n\n### Problem\nA category's topic list shows « Page N » with ‹ › only. #980 (operator, 2026-11-16) wants what the MP list got in #968: a « page x / y » pill with a menu (first, previous, next, last, typed page), shown at the end of the list, hidden when the category has one page. Legacy: `MainWindow.swift:1014-1070` (`ForumTopicsPaginationBar`), `:407-409` (`shouldShowPagination`) @ 87fe0d1c.\n\n### Cause\n`TopicListModel` kept only « a next page exists »; `PageBar` passed `.page(n)` and no `last`/`jump`.\n\n### Change (no second pager: `PagerToolbar`, `PagerPageMenu` and `PagerJump` from #964/#968 are reused untouched)\n- `TopicListContent.pageCount` / `pageCountIsExact`, computed as the MP list does (`MessageListContent.init(page:)`): HFR's last page, at least current + 1 when a next page exists; exact when HFR says so or on the last page.\n- `TopicListModel`: `pageCount`, `canGoToLast`, `goToLastPage`, `goToPage` (clamped when exact, as typed otherwise), `perform(_ jump:)`.\n- `TopicListView.PageBar`: `.pageOf` status, `last`, `jump`, spinner while loading; the bar is hidden on a one-page category (`page > 1 || hasNext`). End-of-list visibility is the existing `pagerBar` (#898). No long press.\n- Flags and favourites stay without a pager (`source.isPaged`).\n- The count is a lower bound when HFR's pager is a window: shown « y+ », and « Dernière page » stays disabled then (rule of `PagerPageMenu`).\n\n### Tests\n`TopicListPagerTests` (new): page count and its lower bound, exactness on the last page, menu steps (first/previous/next/last request sequence), typed page clamped vs as typed, last not offered on a lower bound, disabled states at the bounds, no pager on flags. Not run (Linux session); `compile-check` follows.\n\n### Ledger\n\n```gap-edit\nGAP-024\nSwiftHFR final: « page x / y » pill with its menu (first, previous, next, last, typed page) and ‹ › pills, as the MP list (#968); « y+ » and no « last » while the count is only a lower bound (HFR's pager is a window). The pager shows only when the list is scrolled to its end (or is shorter than the screen), with a short animation (#898); hidden on a one-page category (#980).\n```\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CDvQG8jqNrseTphdnF)_",
